# Daromadchi scheduled jobs — install with `crontab scripts/crontab.example`.
#
# RECONCILED WITH THE LIVE CRONTAB on 2025-08-27. The cadences below are the ones
# actually running on the VPS (`crontab -l`), not proposals. See docs/ops/cron.md.
#
# ── SOURCE-OF-TRUTH FIX (2025-08-27) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# The live crontab called `/var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh` — an UNTRACKED copy
# at the repo root that had drifted from scripts/cron-runner.sh (it no longer wrote
# the per-job logs/ files, and used the `digest` job name). Fix, one command on the
# box, so the crontab runs the version-controlled script and the drift cannot recur:
#
#   ln -sfn scripts/cron-runner.sh /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh
#
# With that symlink in place the paths below (which keep the historical root path so
# the live crontab needs no edit) resolve to the tracked script.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
DAROMADCHI_DIR=/var/www/daromadchi
DAROMADCHI_URL=https://www.daromadchi.uz
MAILTO=""

# Marketplace order/product sync. Orders re-read every tick; heavy work throttled
# per plan inside the route.
*/5 * * * *   /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh sync        >> $HOME/daromadchi-cron.log 2>&1

# Stock write-back for stock_sync shops.
*/5 * * * *   /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh stock-sync  >> $HOME/daromadchi-cron.log 2>&1

# Telegram digests. Live crontab uses the `digest` job name (aliased to
# telegram-digest in cron-runner.sh). The route filters on each seller's own
# notification window, so hourly at :05 is enough to never miss a window.
5 * * * *     /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh digest      >> $HOME/daromadchi-cron.log 2>&1

# Daily housekeeping and the busiest job in the product: expires lapsed plans,
# recomputes derived tiers, sends due price notices, runs free-tier nudges, steps
# the account-lifecycle ladder. Documented at docs/plans/turnover-pricing-spec.md §3.
15 3 * * *    /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh expire-plans >> $HOME/daromadchi-cron.log 2>&1

# Renewals. Charges stored cards, gated by BILLING_AUTORENEW_ENABLED (a no-op with
# that unset). Live cadence is HOURLY at :20 — note this differs from the earlier
# proposal of once-a-day; the route only charges cards actually near expiry.
20 * * * *    /var/www/daromadchi/cron-runner.sh billing-renew >> $HOME/daromadchi-cron.log 2>&1

# ── Watchdog (added 2025-08-27) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# WORK-liveness alarm. Reads the DB directly and pages operators when no sync has
# completed within the expected window — the failure PM2 "online" hides. Its OWN
# line, NOT via cron-runner.sh: cron-runner is HTTP-only and therefore dead exactly
# when the alarm is needed. Depends only on `pg` + node, so it survives a broken app
# build. See docs/ops/monitoring.md.
*/5 * * * *   /var/www/daromadchi/scripts/sync-freshness-check.sh >> $HOME/daromadchi-cron.log 2>&1
